      "writtenOn": "2026-08-04T18:12:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sizing the state from a page count makes sense now the tracker is bigger. I think the count needs a bound though, since the HVC takes it from the host and it reaches `__pkvm_host_donate_hyp()` unchecked. Zero survives the whole path: `range_is_memory(start, start)` tests `start - 1`, `___host_check_page_state_range()` loops zero times, and `pkvm_create_mappings_locked(virt, virt)` maps nothing, so `donate_and_clear_host_page()` returns 0 having donated and cleared nothing. `its_reg-\u003epriv` then points at a page the host still owns and can rewrite, which makes `its-\u003ebase` and the queue pointers host-chosen for the `readq`/`writeq` and `memcpy` in `cwriter_write()`. Could we reject a zero count here?",
      "revId": "35062e70491b0f6d1b2619b050348069ef86cf02",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
